## Original work

The driver code (`smsrio/`, `java/`) is original work by The SMSRio Open Driver
Authors. Its protocol knowledge - message IDs, field layouts, values and the
firmware update sequence - was observed on the device's own USB wire; no vendor
or kernel source is copied, and the code is original work.

## Provenance marker

`smsrio-pbcnx` is a visible provenance/attribution string in the Python package
(`smsrio.PROVENANCE`, printed by `--version`) and in the Java core. It is
intended to make the origin searchable and to encourage the GPL notice to
travel with copies. It is **not** telemetry: it performs no network or device
I/O, carries no user or device identifier, and changes no protocol bytes.
